Cheyenne Fire and Rescue needs to start the process and replace their aging 800 MHz portable radios with newer dual band radios.  Our current
radios will be unable to have a supply of repair parts in 4 to 5 years.  Dual band radios will incorporate both the VHF (Wyo Link) and the 800
MHz public Safety band which will allow for interoperability between city, county and state agencies on a statewide basis.
